{"id":"ae65d3c7-da31-4654-8d4f-d3c21f9156ad","object":"chat.completion","created":1784983107,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    dists = case['distances']\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in dists:\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        w = max(core[u], core[v], d)\\n        edges.append((w, u, v))\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        xr, yr = find(x), find(y)\\n        if xr == yr:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[xr] < rank[yr]:\\n            xr, yr = yr, xr\\n        parent[yr] = xr\\n        if rank[xr] == rank[yr]:\\n            rank[xr] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst = []\\n    total = 0.0\\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst.append([u, v, w])\\n            total += w\\n            if len(mst) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('Graph is not connected')\\n    return {'mst_edges': mst, 'total_weight': total}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to generate Python code for solve(case) that computes the MST of the mutual reachability graph. The case contains nodes list, core_distance dict, distances list of triples (node1, node2, distance). We compute mutual reachability weight = max(core[node1], core[node2], distance). Then run Kruskal's algorithm on the complete graph? But note: The distances list only contains some pairs? Actually, the distances list seems to be all pairs (since it's a complete list of combinations? For 5 nodes, there are 10 pairs, and the fixture shows 10 entries. 